<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Birgi</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Pyrgion</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Birgi is a small town in İzmir province, western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, on the slopes of the Bozdağ mountains. Known in Byzantine times as Pyrgion, it became the first capital of the Aydinid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">beylik</a> in the early 14th century, and its Great Mosque, built in 1312 for Mehmed Bey, survives. Its Ottoman houses, such as the Çakırağa Mansion, are well preserved.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/birgi.jpg" alt="Birgi" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Canel Ölgün · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Birgi_de_yanl%C4%B1z_ev.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
